# IELTS & TOEFL Exam Practice Integration

Add a structured exam practice library to the Typing Studio, with a hierarchical category browser, a Briefing Room (prompt + sample answer), and a Post-Match Analysis panel with vocab/grammar highlights.

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1 — TOEFL Integrated Task (Audio)**
> TOEFL Task 1 requires listening to a lecture audio clip. Should audio be supported in this first version, or should TOEFL Task 1 be text-only for now (lecture summary in text) with audio as a future phase?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2 — Sample Content Source**
> Should the bundled sample essays be written directly into the codebase as a static TypeScript data file (zero-config, works fully offline), or do you want a CMS/admin editor so content can be added without a code deploy?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3 — Vocabulary Highlights**
> In the Post-Match Analysis panel, how should key vocabulary be identified? Option A: **manually tagged** by content author per essay (best quality). Option B: **auto-detected** by CEFR level using the existing `VocabToken` system already in the Coach plugin (no manual authoring).

